Part B — AI Integration Strategy (AI/ML Task)
1. Feature Continuation
Continuing the Smart Expense Categorization feature (Day 10-12). The FastAPI service built on Day 12 (categorization_service.py) remains the core AI service; today's work defines its formal input/output contract and a prototype UI flow for how users will actually interact with it.
2. Input Format
{
  "transaction_id": "string (required)",
  "description": "string (required, non-empty)",
  "amount": "number (required, > 0)",
  "date": "string, YYYY-MM-DD (required)",
  "vendor": "string (optional)"
}
3. Output Format
{
  "transaction_id": "string",
  "status": "success | error",
  "predicted_category": "string | null",
  "confidence": "number | null",
  "error": "string | null",
  "latency_ms": "number"
}
4. Error Handling
•	Validation errors (empty description, non-positive amount) return HTTP 422 with a specific field-level error message before reaching the AI model.
•	Low-confidence predictions (below 0.15 threshold) are not returned as a category — the response explicitly asks for manual selection instead of guessing.
•	Any unexpected internal exception is caught and returned as a structured error response rather than crashing the service.
5. Sample Inputs/Outputs
Sample Input	AI Service Output
{ "transaction_id": "TXN3001", "description": "grocery shopping at Al-Fatah", "amount": 2200, "date": "2026-08-13" }	{ "status": "success", "predicted_category": "Grocery", "confidence": 0.81 }
{ "transaction_id": "TXN3002", "description": "", "amount": 500, "date": "2026-08-13" }	{ "status": "error", "error": "description must not be empty" }
{ "transaction_id": "TXN3003", "description": "zzxxqq unclear text", "amount": 300, "date": "2026-08-13" }	{ "status": "error", "error": "Low model confidence — category needs manual selection" }

6. Prototype UI Flow
Step-by-step flow of how a user experiences this AI feature inside the app:
•	Step 1: User taps 'Add Transaction' and starts typing a description (e.g., 'grocery shopping').
•	Step 2: As soon as the user moves to the next field, the app silently calls the AI Service (/categorize) in the background.
•	Step 3a (success): The Category field auto-fills with the predicted category (e.g., 'Grocery'), shown with a subtle 'AI suggested' label and a small edit icon.
•	Step 3b (low confidence/error): The Category field is left blank/on manual selection, with no visible error shown to the user — the AI simply steps back and lets them pick manually, keeping the experience seamless either way.
•	Step 4: User taps Save. If they changed the suggested category, that correction is silently logged for future model personalization.
7. Integration Points
Mobile Application
Primary integration point. The categorization call happens inline during transaction entry, and also automatically after the OCR receipt-scan flow extracts a description.
Web Application
Same /categorize endpoint is called from the web app's transaction form via the shared backend, giving desktop/web users the identical auto-categorization experience.
Website
Not used for live transaction entry (the marketing website has no ledger), but can showcase this AI feature via a demo/interactive widget so prospective users can see it working before installing the app.
